  <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Learning with purpose.</h1><p>An undergraduate Electrical and Electronic Engineering student at HSTU, Bangladesh, building a thoughtful foundation for practical engineering work, teaching, and future study.</p></header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Academic background</h2><p>Faisal Ahmed Khan is an undergraduate student in Electrical and Electronic Engineering at Hajee Mohammad Danesh Science and Technology University (HSTU), Bangladesh.</p>
    <h2>Current learning interests</h2><p>His current interests include electrical engineering, energy and power systems, and applications of artificial intelligence and machine learning in engineering. These are areas of active learning rather than claims of specialization.</p>
    <h2>Practical engineering projects</h2><p>Alongside academic study, Faisal is building projects step by step to turn technical ideas into clearer, more useful tools. This portfolio records the intended scope, current status, and next steps of that work without overstating outcomes.</p>
    <h2>Teaching &amp; explanation</h2><p>He is interested in teaching and in explaining technical concepts clearly. Over time, this site will collect learning notes, educational material, and project reflections that support that interest.</p>
    <h2>Long-term direction</h2><p>Faisal is interested in graduate study and future research opportunities in engineering. He is developing his academic foundation, project experience, and ability to communicate technical ideas in preparation for that path.</p>
